    "https://careers.umassd.edu/en-us/job/529966/parttime-lecturer-political-science": {
      "title": "Jobs at UMass Dartmouth | Details - Part-Time Lecturer - Political Science",
      "description": "Jobs at UMass Dartmouth | Details - Part-Time Lecturer - Political Science Skip to main content Support UMassD Directory Check My Status myUMassD University of Massachusetts Dartmouth Search UMass Dartmouth Menu About Admissions Academics Research Outreach Student Life Athletics Alumni & Friends Jobs at UMass Dartmouth Toggle navigation from this section Toggle share controls Share on Facebook Share this on X Share on LinkedIn Print this page Email this page Copy URL Link copied to clipboard! University of Massachusetts Dartmouth HOME About // Administration // Human Resources // Jobs at UMass Dartmouth Close Jobs at UMass Dartmouth A great place to work UMass Dartmouth is a vibrant university dedicated to engaged learning and innovative research. Join us in our mission to support student success, foster academic excellence, and promote diverse collaboration. UMassD is a great place to work! Search by keyword Part-Time Lecturer - Political Science Apply now Job no: 529966 Work type: Faculty Part Time/Adjunct, Faculty Part Time - Talent Community Categories: Faculty Position Overview The Department of Political Science at UMass Dartmouth is inviting expressions of interest for a part-time lecturer position. We are particularly interested in candidates who are prepared to teach introductory courses in Comparative Politics. While this is the primary focus, the ability to teach other political science courses, such as introductory International Relations, is considered a plus. The courses are primarily in-person, although some online sections may be available. Qualifications A PhD in Political Science is preferred. ABD candidates with relevant teaching experience will be considered. Our Values The College of Arts and Sciences and the Department of Political Science value the ability to serve students from a broad range of cultural heritages and socioeconomic backgrounds. We seek a teaching faculty member who values working in a collegial, collaborative environment, guided by a commitment to helping all students achieve their educational goals. How to Express Interest Expressions of interest are reviewed on a rolling basis. Please submit a cover letter, CV, and the names of two references. About UMass Dartmouth UMass Dartmouth has transformed the lives of 40,000 alumni and distinguishes itself as a vibrant, public research university dedicated to engaged learning and innovative research. It is the only Massachusetts Tier 1 national research university south of Boston. Located on a beautiful 710-acre suburban campus on the South Coast of Massachusetts, UMass Dartmouth offers faculty the opportunity to work alongside talented students and colleagues in a community defined by genuine support and dedication. Advertised: 10 Jul 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Great, we can send you jobs like this, if this is your first time signing up, please check your inbox to confirm your subscription. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Closes Part-Time Lecturer - Political Science The University of Massachusetts Dartmouth is looking for talented individuals with an interest in working as Political Science  Part-Time Lecturers in the Political Science Department. Current opportunities Position Closes Part-Time Lecturer - Political Science The University of Massachusetts Dartmouth is looking for talented individuals with an interest in working as Political Science  Part-Time Lecturers in the Political Science Department. Expression of interest No expression of interest currently available Powered by PageUp The University of Massachusetts Dartmouth welcomes all qualified applicants and complies with all state and federal anti-discrimination laws. Clery Discl